  "action": "Admission-threshold redesign decision (Candidate #3 round 2). Evaluated receiver-boundary design vs endogenous observational design. Boundary design (impose m=1.3 control / m=1.5 intervention at adapter boundary, same DR seed) is clean: isolates receiver quantization, preserves DR unchanged, uses only naturally-reachable multipliers (rejected m=2.0 as hypothetical). Observational design rejected (sticky multiplier limits variation; m=1.5 co-moves with war/weather confounds; baseAdmit not independent of events). m=1.5 analysis: P(baseAdmit=2)=1/3, +0.333 admissions/tick, ~+6.7 over 20 ticks. Primary endpoint = admission count (not occupancy/mortality; discharge closed). Verdict: FREEZE BOUNDARY PROTOCOL. Relation to Phase F: orthogonal (B vs C), complementary. No experiment run; no model/manuscript/QMS changes."
}